<title>UK: BP, PETRONAS TO BUILD ACETIC ACID PLANT.</title>
<headline>BP, PETRONAS TO BUILD ACETIC ACID PLANT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Petroleum and Malysia's Petronas Nasional Berhad will build a venture acetic acid plant in Kertih, Malaysia.</p>
<p>The $150 million plant is scheduled to be onstream by the end of 1999, BP said.</p>
<p>BP will have a 70 percent stake in the joint venture owning the plant, while Petronas will hold the remainder.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 71 542 7717</p>
</text>
